WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:01.756
- [Instructor] The fifth century in Greece

00:00:01.756 --> 00:00:03.611
started off with the Persian invasions,

00:00:03.611 --> 00:00:05.800
and ended with the Peloponnesian War,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.018
and now we're entering into
the fourth century in Greece.

00:00:09.018 --> 00:00:12.035
And as we enter into the fourth century,

00:00:12.035 --> 00:00:14.290
Thebes is the dominant city state,

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.083
but as we get into the mid fourth century,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.666
and especially the end of it,

00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:21.667
we will see that all of
Greece gets dominated,

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:25.934
and then unified, by the
Makedonians, or the Macedonians,

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:29.437
and in particular, the first unifier here

00:00:29.437 --> 00:00:31.866
was Philip of Macedon.

00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:33.338
This is a bust of him.

00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:37.338
And he's known, as he
comes to power in 359 BCE,

00:00:39.168 --> 00:00:42.752
he comes to power, his
father was king of Makedon,

00:00:42.752 --> 00:00:46.526
but then his older
brothers die, he becomes,

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:49.541
it's actually his nephew
who is heir to the throne.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:52.737
He becomes regent for his infant nephew,

00:00:52.737 --> 00:00:54.796
which means that he has
the power temporarily,

00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:56.923
but then he actually takes full control,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.707
and becomes king of Macedon, or Makedon,

00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:02.790
as it's often pronounced, in 359 BCE.

00:01:03.935 --> 00:01:07.814
And what he then goes off about doing is

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:11.489
taking over most of the Greek city states.

00:01:11.489 --> 00:01:13.617
And, eventually, he's able to unify

00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:15.987
most of the Greek city states.

00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:18.399
And you can see on this map here,

00:01:18.399 --> 00:01:20.469
which I got from Wikipedia.

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:23.610
This is a little bit of
information about the map.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.508
You can see how he expanded
his empire over time.

00:01:28.508 --> 00:01:33.124
Remember, 359 BCE, he
becomes king of Macedon.

00:01:33.124 --> 00:01:35.957
In 352, he's moving into Thessaly.

00:01:39.077 --> 00:01:42.577
Then, in the 340s, he's going into Thrace.

00:01:44.793 --> 00:01:48.730
So he's going into Thrace and Molossia.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.252
And Molossia's interesting.

00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:54.461
The king of Molossia, he
actually ends up marrying

00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:57.493
the king of Molossia's daughter, Olympius,

00:01:57.493 --> 00:02:00.811
who ends up being Alexander
the Great's mother.

00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:02.453
And she's a pretty interesting character,

00:02:02.453 --> 00:02:03.510
as we will see in a little bit.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.574
She was part of this cult
that worshiped snakes.

00:02:06.574 --> 00:02:09.536
It's believed that she slept with snakes.

00:02:09.536 --> 00:02:13.255
But, he goes off and continues to conquer.

00:02:13.255 --> 00:02:15.702
Eventually, he's able to subjugate

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.051
most of the city states of Greece,

00:02:18.051 --> 00:02:19.884
except for Sparta.

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:23.384
And that takes us to 337, right over here,

00:02:26.892 --> 00:02:30.112
where he's able to establish
the League of Corinth.

00:02:30.112 --> 00:02:31.566
It was only called the League of Corinth

00:02:31.566 --> 00:02:33.875
after the fact, but he gets the leaders

00:02:33.875 --> 00:02:37.291
of the significant city
states together in Corinth.

00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:39.153
That's why it's called
the League of Corinth,

00:02:39.153 --> 00:02:41.617
and they swear their oath, essentially,

00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:46.267
to Philip, king of Makedon,
who they call the Hegemon.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.088
And what's really important about that

00:02:48.088 --> 00:02:51.546
is he's able to unify
the Greek city states,

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:53.046
outside of Sparta,

00:02:54.622 --> 00:02:58.101
and in doing so, he sets
things up for his son,

00:02:58.101 --> 00:03:00.657
the famous Alexander the Great,

00:03:00.657 --> 00:03:02.610
to continue to unify Greece.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.793
Alexander the Great's actually
able to subjugate Sparta.

00:03:05.793 --> 00:03:08.973
But then, more famously,
he goes off to conquer

00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:12.341
the entire Persian
Empire, and then beyond,

00:03:12.341 --> 00:03:13.410
in his short life.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:16.197
And we'll have at least
another video on that.

00:03:16.197 --> 00:03:19.098
But just to get a feel for what happened

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:22.098
at the League of Corinth in 337 BCE,

00:03:23.062 --> 00:03:24.895
I will share this oath

00:03:27.697 --> 00:03:31.339
that the variouscity
states had to commit to.

00:03:31.339 --> 00:03:35.132
And it says, "I swear
by Zeus, Gaia, Helios,

00:03:35.132 --> 00:03:37.743
"Poseidon, and all the gods and goddesses.

00:03:37.743 --> 00:03:40.125
"I will abide by the common peace,

00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:42.870
"and I will neither break
the agreement with Philip,

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.404
"nor take up arms on land or sea,

00:03:45.404 --> 00:03:48.474
"harming any of those
abiding by the oaths.

00:03:48.474 --> 00:03:51.106
"Nor shall I take any city or fortress,

00:03:51.106 --> 00:03:53.784
"nor harbor by craft or contrivance,

00:03:53.784 --> 00:03:57.389
"with intent of war against
the participants of the war.

00:03:57.389 --> 00:03:59.205
"Nor shall I depose the kingship

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:01.083
"of Philip or his descendants,

00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:03.605
"nor the constitutions
existing in each state,

00:04:03.605 --> 00:04:06.157
"when they swore the oaths of the peace.

00:04:06.157 --> 00:04:08.854
"Nor shall I do anything
contrary to these agreements,

00:04:08.854 --> 00:04:11.774
"nor shall I allow anyone
else, as far as possible.

00:04:11.774 --> 00:04:14.564
"But if anyone does commit
any breach of the treaty,

00:04:14.564 --> 00:04:17.659
"I shall go in support as
called by those who need,

00:04:17.659 --> 00:04:20.790
"and I shall fight the
transgressors of the common peace,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.957
"as decided by the council,
and called on by the Hegemon."

00:04:27.144 --> 00:04:31.311
Who is, when the oath is made,
who is Philip of Macedonia.

00:04:33.514 --> 00:04:37.718
Now, unfortunately for
Philip, this happens in 337,

00:04:37.718 --> 00:04:40.997
where, for the most part,
he's the first to unify

00:04:40.997 --> 00:04:44.137
the Greek city states, outside of Sparta.

00:04:44.137 --> 00:04:46.989
But he's only able to live
about a year after that.

00:04:46.989 --> 00:04:49.906
A year later, we're now in 336 BCE,

00:04:52.112 --> 00:04:56.651
and he's in the old capitol
of the Makedonian kingdom,

00:04:56.651 --> 00:04:58.998
which is very close to Pella,

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:02.085
celebrating the wedding of his daughter

00:05:02.085 --> 00:05:03.918
to his brother in law.

00:05:05.155 --> 00:05:08.750
So his daughter, who
is Alexander's sister,

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.070
she's being married to Olympius's brother.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:15.446
So he's marrying his
daughter to her uncle.

00:05:15.446 --> 00:05:18.088
And it is during that wedding that

00:05:18.088 --> 00:05:22.027
Philip of Macedon is killed by Pausanias,

00:05:22.027 --> 00:05:24.025
who is his bodyguard.

00:05:24.025 --> 00:05:26.323
And there's a lot of
really interesting stories.

00:05:26.323 --> 00:05:30.023
So, he's killed at the wedding in 336 BCE,

00:05:30.023 --> 00:05:31.580
and there's a lot of
really interesting stories

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.323
about what the motivation
for Pausanias was.

00:05:34.323 --> 00:05:36.075
There are many accounts that say that

00:05:36.075 --> 00:05:38.457
Pausanias was Philip's lover,

00:05:38.457 --> 00:05:40.654
he was, on some level jealous,

00:05:40.654 --> 00:05:43.010
and he was on some level because

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:46.139
another relative of Philip
affronted Pausanias,

00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:47.802
and Philip didn't go to defend him.

00:05:47.802 --> 00:05:51.348
There's some narratives that
this was arranged, somehow,

00:05:51.348 --> 00:05:55.515
by Olympius, Philip's wife
and the mother of Alexander,

00:05:56.618 --> 00:05:59.242
to put Alexander on the throne.

00:05:59.242 --> 00:06:01.037
There're some motivations there because,

00:06:01.037 --> 00:06:03.865
also, shortly before the assassination,

00:06:03.865 --> 00:06:07.682
he took a second wife, which
was his more favored wife,

00:06:07.682 --> 00:06:09.142
as opposed to Olympius.

00:06:09.142 --> 00:06:11.325
So there's a lot of really
interesting accounts,

00:06:11.325 --> 00:06:13.307
and I encourage you to read up on it.

00:06:13.307 --> 00:06:14.814
But the interesting thing is,

00:06:14.814 --> 00:06:17.314
is after he gets assassinated,

00:06:18.256 --> 00:06:22.729
well, then there's a bit
of a scramble for power.

00:06:22.729 --> 00:06:25.774
But it leaves Alexander the Great,

00:06:25.774 --> 00:06:28.851
or eventually, Alexander
the Third officially,

00:06:28.851 --> 00:06:30.623
but eventually Alexander the Great

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.290
becomes the Hegemon,

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.935
and he's eventually, in his short life,

00:06:34.935 --> 00:06:38.451
he's only 20 years old
when he becomes king,

00:06:38.451 --> 00:06:41.667
he's able to, as we'll see
in the next few videos,

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:45.000
take over all of the
Persian Empire and beyond,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.274
and subjugate Sparta.

00:06:46.274 --> 00:06:48.469
So he further unifies the Greeks,

00:06:48.469 --> 00:06:51.719
and takes on the mighty Persian Empire.

